grab your cave and gear and don't get  frightened because we have the most  thrilling film about cave since Journey  to the Center of the Earth  the descent is one of my all-time  favorite horror films so in this video  we're gonna take a deep dive into its  ending and some of the things you might  have missed along the way I'll also be  going over the differences between the  UK and US theatrical versions because  one ending in my opinion is way better  than the other at its surface the  descent is a film about a group of women  who struggled to escape a cave system  infested with ravenous creatures known  as crawlers but what this film is really  about is one woman's struggle to  overcome the pain of losing her daughter  in the beginning of the film our  protagonist sara is out whitewater  rafting with two of her friends Juno and  Beth while her husband and daughter  watch from the side this is a great  setup since it establishes everyone's  relationship to one another while  simultaneously showing us that they're  thrill-seekers the rafting also  juxtaposes the quaint car ride in the  next scene where we as the viewer have  let our guard down only for a huge jump  scare to occur which sets the story in  motion the death of Sarah's husband and  daughter but even before this event the  writer and director are setting up key  hints that will pay off later in the  film mainly how Sarah's husband Peter  was having an affair with Juno for  example when the ladies get off the raft  Juno immediately goes to Peter who helps  her take off her helmet this interaction  is clocked by Beth who gives us somewhat  worrying look hinting that she too  either knows about the affair or at  least suspects something in the car  moments before the crash Sarah says to  Peter you can't you seem a bit distant  clearly something is on Peters mind and  this something is his infidelity it's  also in this scene that Sarah has a  throw off line telling her daughter  Jessica that when they get home they can  plan her birthday party it's this  birthday cake and image of her daughter  which becomes a recurring motif that  haunts Sarah throughout the story waking  up in the hospital the only survivor of  the crash  Sarah experiences her first  hallucination with the lights in the  hospital turning off behind her as she's  thrust back into reality by her friends  learning of the death of her husband and  daughter  now this scene is also interesting  because Juno here instead of rushing to  console her friend like Beth does she  simply leaves not just the hospital but  the entire country without even saying  goodbye to Sara likely feeling guilty  over her affair with Paul in his death  as will later find out Juno and Paul's  affair wasn't just a one-time fling they  loved each other as evidenced by the  necklace Paul gave her which we'll get  to in a bit the crash also had another  effect on Sara drug addiction and it's  quite easy to miss the drugs in question  seem to help Sara with PTSD from the  crash and to help her cope with the loss  of her child we only see her take these  pills once after she experiences a  nightmare about the crash a nightmare  which is accompanied by giggles from her  daughter as we flash forward one year to  the appellations the adventuresome girls  gather to take on a cave and one of the  girls Holly says this to Sara always  searching for the next big hi sorry Sara  immediately thinks Holly's hi is  referring to her drugs when in fact it's  just the high of adrenaline you  experienced when doing extreme sports  Juno also has a picture taken by Paul  with the inscription love each day this  saying is later found engraved on Juno's  necklace which was a present from Paul  and it's how Sara later finds out Juno  was fooling around with her husband  there's also another subtle hint that  the girls know about the affair  when Juno comes in and says this line to  Sam and Holly Sam's response here is  really weird  what once is she referring to this is  yet another subtle clue that proves the  other girls knew about Juno's affair  the girls eventually make their way to  what they believe is an easy cave system  called Boreham caverns but little do  they know Juno has done away with a  guidebook and taken them to an uncharted  system  she has withheld this information and  lied to them just like what she did with  Sara and her affair with Paul as they  make their way to the cave Rebecca  Lissa's series of side effects cavers  might experience while caving  dehydration disorientation the inclusion  of paranoia and hallucinations here are  really important because Sarah will be  increasingly plagued by visions of her  daughter as this story and her paranoia  progress there's even some foreshadowing  of the carnage to come with weird blood  marks near the caves entrance and the  mutilated body of a dead deer deers are  known as symbols of trust and to see one  mutilated here is a reference to the  broken trust between Juno and Sarah  there are also symbols of new adventure  hence the start of their expedition but  their adventure takes a turn when the  cave collapses leaving them trapped  below with creatures known as the  crawlers not much is known about them  but they have evolved perfectly to live  in the dark completely blind using sound  to communicate with one another their  bodies have adapted to be able to climb  the caves jagged walls and easily  traverse its many cramped spaces but  perhaps the most shocking moment of the  movie happens when Juno accidentally  kills Beth mistaking her from one of the  crawlers instead of staying there with  her Juno leaves just like she left after  the death of Paul but before Juno leaves  Beth is able to rip off her necklace  which will later be discovered by Sarah  confirming Juno's affair with her  husband it's this revelation combined  with the fact Juno left Beth to die that  compels Sarah to stab Juno with her  pickaxe in the leg leaving her to defend  herself against the approaching crawlers  with Sarah being the only survivor left  she makes her way to the caves second  entrance a second entrance which was  discovered by the girls through ancient  Native American cave paintings buried  deep within the cave that combined with  old markers left by a previous caving  expedition from the early 1900's who  never made it out  Sarah is able to find her way but here's  where things get really interesting  right before Sarah makes her way out she  falls down a small pit and is knocked  unconscious for a few seconds and it's  at this time the lighting switches from  her torch to daylight now this can be  interpreted in two ways that the  daylight just happens to shine in that  exact moment or that this is her  transitioning into a hallucination and I  think it's a lot  of the two we know from earlier that  sarah only experiences these  hallucinations when she's either  sleeping or knocked unconscious earlier  in the film when Sarah nearly makes it  out of the cave collapse  she's briefly incapacitated and  experiences a vision of her daughter  with the birthday cake these moments  where her head gets bonked around seems  to trigger these visions the second  reason I believe it's hallucination has  to do with the UK version of the ending  so here's where the US theatrical and UK  endings slightly differ in both versions  Sarah makes her way out of the cave into  the car and stops by the side of the  road after letting out a bit of her  lunch she composes herself only to find  the ghost of Juno beside her that's  where the US version ends but if you  watched the UK version this story  continues Sarah wakes up back in the  cave in the same position right when she  was knocked unconscious the whole escape  from the cave was all in her mind just  like her daughter who is now in front of  her with the birthday cake but as the  camera pushes back we see there is no  daughter no birthday cake it was all in  her imagination as the sounds of the  crawlers intensify around her this  ending was deemed too dark for American  audiences and thus was cut from the  theatrical release I prefer the UK  ending because it wraps up Sarah's  character and pays off the visions of  her daughter which were built up  throughout the film  but what ending do you guys prefer also  this is my first attempt at going back  and doing older movies so I want to hear  your thoughts should I do more like this  and if so what should I do next make  sure to LIKE and subscribe and go ahead  and follow me on Twitter for the latest  updates at the Bing story YT until next  time remember daddy loves you very much

